{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_std_1_safestan`, `y_std_2_safestan`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the original model computed `y_std = (y - mean(y)) / sd(y)` in `transformed data` and then scored that transformed-data quantity twice. SafeStan requires observed variables on the left side of sampling statements to be top-level protected data, and each protected variable may be scored exactly once. The safe model adds two top-level protected vectors, each a deterministic copy of the standardized response, and uses the two original normal likelihood terms once each. In `data_safe.json`, `y_std_1_safestan = y_std_2_safestan = (y - mean(y)) / sd(y)`, using Stan's sample standard deviation, computed from the supplied `y`. The original predictors `x` and `z` remain unprotected context inputs and their standardization is unchanged. Parameter priors are unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  vector[N] y;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] z;
  vector[N] y_std_1_safestan;
  vector[N] y_std_2_safestan;
}
transformed data {
  vector[N] x_std;
  vector[N] z_std;

  x_std = (x - mean(x)) / sd(x);
  z_std = (z - mean(z)) / sd(z);
  print("pines_independant");
}
parameters {
  real alpha;
  real beta;
  real gamma;
  real delta;
  vector<lower=0>[2] sigma;
}
model {
  array[2] vector[N] mu;

  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 5);
  mu[1] = alpha + beta * x_std;

  gamma ~ normal(0, 10);
  delta ~ normal(0, 5);
  mu[2] = gamma + delta * z_std;

  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 5);

  // estimate separately
  y_std_1_safestan ~ normal(mu[1], sigma[1]);
  y_std_2_safestan ~ normal(mu[2], sigma[2]);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":2,"x":[3.7768106627284297,0.2],"y":[2.0,0.0],"z":[2.1238757838833973,0.2],"y_std_1_safestan":[0.7071067811865475,-0.7071067811865475],"y_std_2_safestan":[0.7071067811865475,-0.7071067811865475]}","protected_variables":["y_std_1_safestan","y_std_2_safestan"]}
